  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cash For Trash &amp; Waste Education for 200 Families</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bali has a massive waste problem, starting at the household level where plastic and organic matter is thrown away as trash. Our waste education and recycling program trains 200 families to use less plastic, generate less waste and recycle. Working with a local recycling company, Bumi Sehat and a local women&apos;s group organizes monthly trash-for-cash collections and student waste education programs. This results in less waste going to landfills, more household income &amp; awareness of waste issues.</narrative>
  </description>
